---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Nav from "../components/Nav.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
---
<BaseLayout title="LinerFM: Privacy Policy" description="LinerFM runs on Mac and Windows. No account, no telemetry in the app. The website uses the TikTok pixel only if you accept it.">
  <Nav />
  <main id="main-content" class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-5 py-16">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em]">Privacy Policy</h1>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-lg font-semibold">The app</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-fg-2">LinerFM runs on your Mac or Windows PC and has no account system. The app contacts our server to check your trial or license, and when you send a bug report.</p>
    <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-fg-2 text-sm list-disc pl-5">
      <li>Your Spotify and Groq API keys are stored locally on your device and used only to call those services directly from your computer.</li>
      <li>Your listening history and playlist data never leave your machine.</li>
      <li>The app sends no telemetry and no usage data.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-lg font-semibold">This website</h2>
    <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-fg-2 text-sm list-disc pl-5">
      <li>We count page views and download clicks with an anonymous per-tab id, without cookies: we store the page, the site you came from, whether you are on a phone or a computer, the country and the time, never your IP address or other browser details.</li>
      <li>On a phone you can leave your email to get the download link for your Mac or PC. We store the address, the country, the time and which site sent you here, and use it only to send you that link. It is deleted after 30 days at most, and never shared.</li>
      <li>We use the TikTok pixel to measure which TikTok ads bring visitors here and whether they lead to a purchase. It runs only if you click <strong>Accept</strong> in the cookie banner. If you decline, or don't choose, nothing is loaded from TikTok and no cookie is set.</li>
      <li><strong>If you accept:</strong> the pixel (provided by TikTok) sets the <code>_ttp</code> cookie and reports page views and clicks on the Buy button. If you arrived from a TikTok ad, the click identifier in the link (<code>ttclid</code>) is kept in your browser's local storage.</li>
      <li><strong>If you then buy:</strong> we pass your consent, <code>_ttp</code> and <code>ttclid</code> to the checkout. When the order is paid, our license server sends TikTok a purchase event with the order number, the total and currency, and your email address and customer number hashed with SHA-256 (TikTok receives the hash, not the address).</li>
      <li><strong>Legal basis:</strong> your consent. You can withdraw it at any time with the button below. We then delete the cookie and the stored click identifier, and future purchases are not reported.</li>
      <li>TikTok processes this data under its own <a href="https://www.tiktok.com/legal/page/global/tiktok-business-privacy-policy/en" class="underline underline-offset-2 text-white">Business Products privacy policy</a>.</li>
    </ul>
    <button type="button" data-cookie-settings class="btn-ghost mt-6 rounded-xl px-4 py-2.5 text-sm font-semibold">Cookie settings</button>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-lg font-semibold">Payments</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-fg-2 text-sm">Payments are processed by Lemon Squeezy (our Merchant of Record); their privacy policy governs the checkout.</p>

    <p class="mt-8 text-xs text-fg-3">Last updated: 2026-10-18. Questions: open an issue on GitHub.</p>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
